    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` derived field on the owner response so it reports `true` when **any** of the three risk signals holds, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the owner schema (the DTO is generated from this at build time), documenting the three conditions.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Set `riskFlag` on every response path that already sets the sibling warning flags (`getOwner`, the idempotent-replay branch of `addOwner`, and the created-owner branch), and added the computing helpers:\n   - `isRiskFlagActive(owner)` \u2014 ORs the three signals.\n   - **possible duplicate** \u2192 reuses the existing `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()`.\n   - **city over soft capacity** \u2192 `isCityOverSoftCapacity`, true once the city holds at least the soft/warning threshold (`CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` = 40), grouping cities with the same normalization as the existing capacity rules.\n   - **disposable-adjacent email** \u2192 `isDisposableAdjacentEmail`, true when the email domain is a subdomain of a blocklisted disposable provider (e.g. `mail.mailinator.com`) or shares a provider's registrable base label under a different TLD (e.g. `tempmail.io`). Exact blocklist domains are already rejected at create, so this deliberately covers the near-misses. A null/blank email is never flagged.\n\nThe result is always set explicitly, so it serializes as `false` rather than null \u2014 matching `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`, which creates a structured owner (no email, unique city/name) and asserts `$.riskFlag == false`.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
